{
  "$schema": "https://turbo.build/schema.json",
  // globalEnv is a CACHE-CORRECTNESS list, not a documentation list: a variable
  // that changes what `build`/`test`/`typecheck` PRODUCE must be here, or turbo
  // will serve a hit computed under a different environment. The main-kind
  // gate (`ctl gate <sha>`, before a merge to main) runs --force and would never
  // see such a hit; the release-kind gate (`ctl gate <sha> --base release/<x>`,
  // a task landing) runs with the cache ON, so there it would show up — and so
  // would T14's CI job, which persists the cache.
  //
  // PLAN 11 TASK 1 added nine variables to apps/server/src/config.ts and NONE
  // of them belongs here. The reason is the same for all nine and it is a
  // measured one, not a judgement: their only reader is
  // `loadConfig(process.env)` in apps/server/src/index.ts, the boot path, which
  // no turbo task invokes. Every test that exercises them passes an explicit
  // object to loadConfig, and `apps/server/test/config.test.ts` reads
  // `.env.example` as a FILE. Swept over apps/, packages/ and scripts/ for each
  // name: the only occurrence outside config.ts and .env.example is a prose
  // mention of `RATE_LIMIT_*` in a docblock.
  //
  //   TRUST_PROXY, RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_MAX, RATE_LIMIT_EVENTS_MAX,
  //   RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_SEC, ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL, SMTP_URL, MAGIC_LINK_FROM,
  //   DATABASE_CA_CERT, DEPLOY_SHA
  //     — no build, test or typecheck reads any of them from the environment,
  //       so listing them would add nine spurious cache misses and no coverage.
  //
  // DEPLOY_SHA deserves its own sentence because it is the one that could look
  // like it belongs: it is a build-identity variable, and those usually are
  // baked in. Here it is not — /healthz reads it at RUNTIME from the config the
  // process booted with, so it changes no artifact. If a later task ever bakes
  // it into a bundle (the NEXT_PUBLIC_ pattern two lines below), it must move
  // into this list in the same change, and turbo 2's default envMode:strict is
  // what makes that necessary rather than optional — an undeclared variable
  // reaches such a task as `undefined`, which for DEPLOY_SHA silently becomes
  // the 'dev' default instead of failing.
  // THE ONE ROOT FILE EVERY PACKAGE READS. Every package's tsconfig `extends`
  // `../../tsconfig.base.json`, and turbo hashes only a package's OWN files, so an
  // edit to the base (a `strict` flag, a `target`, a `paths` entry) left every
  // build, typecheck and test replaying a green log computed under the old
  // compiler options. MEASURED 2026-10-02 against this repo's `--dry=json`: the
  // global hash's `files` map was EMPTY. The release-kind gate caches, so this is
  // no longer hypothetical.
  "globalDependencies": ["tsconfig.base.json"],
  "globalEnv": [
    "DATABASE_URL",
    "TEST_DATABASE_ADMIN_URL",
    "NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL",
    "SERVER_ORIGIN"
  ],
  "tasks": {
    "build": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "outputs": ["dist/**", ".next/**", "!.next/cache/**"]
    },
    // The RN webview bundle: ONE html file, gitignored (`dist-webview/`), read by
    // `apps/mobile`'s test through `generate-editor-html.mjs --check`. Nothing in
    // the gate built it before, so a stale copy left on disk by an earlier
    // `build:webview` produced a false STALE (2026-10-02 01:07, the BRD-08 gate)
    // — and, worse, a CLEAN checkout produced a false "no-bundle" skip: `--check`
    // warns and exits 0 when the bundle is absent. Now it is a graph task of its
    // own with declared outputs, so turbo rebuilds it when `packages/editor`'s
    // inputs change and restores it from the cache when they did not.
    "build:webview": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "outputs": ["dist-webview/**"]
    },
    "test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"]
    },
    // `apps/mobile`'s `test` begins with `generate-editor-html.mjs --check`, which
    // diffs `packages/editor/dist-webview/index.html` (the task above) against the
    // checked-in `src/editor/editor-html.generated.ts`. The dependency is what makes
    // the bundle exist and be CURRENT before the check reads it; and because turbo
    // folds a dependency task's hash into the dependent's, a change to
    // `packages/editor`'s CSS or source also changes THIS task's hash — it is the
    // only way the cache sees a bundle it never reads as a file. `$TURBO_DEFAULT$`
    // is the checked-in generated file, which is mobile's own. The measured trace of
    // this package's tests found no other read outside it (2026-10-02).
    "@gisik-nokma/mobile#test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build", "@gisik-nokma/editor#build:webview"],
      "inputs": ["$TURBO_DEFAULT$"]
    },
    // `packages/ui`'s token-discipline suite READS EVERY CLIENT SOURCE TREE FROM
    // DISK (`test/helpers/colour-scan.ts`, via `REPO_ROOT`), so its correct inputs
    // are not its own package. Without this, turbo scopes the hash to
    // `packages/ui/**` and a colour literal added anywhere it polices leaves the
    // cache VALID — the task replays a green log and the violation ships.
    //
    // MEASURED 2026-09-07, which is why this entry exists: with the cache warm, a
    // real `#b3261e` planted in `apps/web/src/shell-refusal.tsx` produced
    // "cache hit, replaying logs … FULL TURBO", exit 0. The same violation under
    // direct `vitest` exits 1 and names the file. **The scanner was never wrong;
    // the gate could not see it.** That is how `#270` reached `main` — the gate on
    // its own PR was genuinely green because this task never re-ran.
    //
    // `$TURBO_ROOT$` (turbo 2.x) is what lets a package declare inputs outside
    // itself. `$TURBO_DEFAULT$` keeps the package's own files as well; listing
    // only the foreign trees would silence changes to the scanner itself.
    //
    // THE LITERAL-TREE ENTRIES ARE A COPY OF `CLIENT_SOURCE_ROOTS`, and a copy that
    // stops matching is exactly the defect this repo names elsewhere — so it is not
    // left to discipline: `token-discipline.test.ts` PARSES this file and asserts the
    // two agree, the same way case 13.208 asserts `ci.yml`'s parsed job graph rather
    // than its text.
    //
    // THE FOUR WILDCARD ENTRIES (`apps/*/test/**` ... `packages/*/package.json`) ARE A
    // DIFFERENT READER IN THE SAME SUITE, found by tracing its real fs reads
    // (2026-10-02, when the release-kind gate began to cache): the "no package's tests
    // read outside itself" case reads EVERY package's `test/` tree and `package.json`
    // to find the escapers. Cached against the client trees alone, a new escaping test
    // in `packages/domain/test` would leave this guard replaying green over the one
    // file it exists to read.
    "@gisik-nokma/ui#test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "inputs": [
        "$TURBO_DEFAULT$",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/turbo.json",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/ui/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/app-core/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/editor/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/app/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/desktop/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/mobile/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/knowledge-graph/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/*/test/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/*/test/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/*/package.json",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/*/package.json"
      ]
    },
    // KG-C T1: the browser suite drives Chromium against the BUILT knowledge-graph package and reads the stylesheet the view ships.
    "@gisik-nokma/knowledge-graph-browser#test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      // The Playwright port (13.2280, 27.360): `ctl gate` exports KG_PW_PORT=3291 and turbo's strict env mode would drop it. A pass-through variable is
      // not hashed, so the port changes no cache key.
      "passThroughEnv": ["KG_PW_PORT"],
      "inputs": ["$TURBO_DEFAULT$", "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/knowledge-graph/src/**", "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/ui/src/ui.css"]
    },
    // kg-walk-fixes item 3 (27.078): `harness/sheet-errors.tsx` imports the web app's `globals.css` and `shell-refusal.tsx`, and
    // `apps/web` is not this package's dependency, so `^build` never folds them into the hash: without these an edit to either
    // replayed a cached green.
    "@gisik-nokma/workflow-canvas-browser#test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "inputs": ["$TURBO_DEFAULT$", "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/app/globals.css", "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/src/shell-refusal.tsx"]
    },
    // The same hole in `typecheck` (13.1719): this package's tsconfig includes `harness`, so tsc follows
    // `harness/sheet-errors.tsx` into `shell-refusal.tsx` (`tsc --listFiles` lists it), and a change to ShellRefusal's props
    // must re-check the harness. Only `inputs` differ from the generic `typecheck`. `globals.css` is left out: it carries no
    // types (`vite/client` declares `*.css`), so it cannot change what tsc reports.
    "@gisik-nokma/workflow-canvas-browser#typecheck": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "inputs": ["$TURBO_DEFAULT$", "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/src/shell-refusal.tsx"]
    },
    // `reporting-scope-guard.test.ts` walks SEVEN trees (its own `SCANNED_ROOTS`),
    // and three CSS-binding suites read `packages/ui/src/ui.css` — the stylesheet
    // whose class names they assert against rendered markup. A rule deleted from
    // `ui.css` would leave every one of them replaying a green log.
    //
    // THE BROAD `apps/**` + `packages/**` ENTRIES (traced 2026-10-02) are the help
    // suite: `help/*.test.ts` run `scripts/help-content.mjs`, whose "quoted strings are
    // still in the product" check greps EVERY .ts/.tsx/.js/.mjs/.css/.json/.md file
    // under `apps/` and `packages/` for the strings `docs/manual.md` quotes. A string
    // deleted from any screen in any package can turn that red, so this task's honest
    // input set is the whole product tree and it will miss on almost any code change.
    // That is the correct answer: the alternatives are a list that omits the file that
    // broke it, or `cache: false`, which would also forget that a docs-only change
    // cannot affect it. The `!` entries are NOT optional: turbo's globs walk the disk,
    // not git, so without them the hash swallows every gitignored build output under
    // `apps/` and `packages/` (measured: 3431 of 5606 hashed files were `dist/`,
    // `.next/` and `.turbo/*.log`), and a task whose inputs include its own previous
    // run's timestamps never hits the cache. They mirror the walker's own
    // `PRODUCT_SKIP` in `scripts/help-content.mjs`.
    "@gisik-nokma/app-core#test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "inputs": [
        "$TURBO_DEFAULT$",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/app-core/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/domain/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/rule-engine/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/ui/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/server/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/app/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**/node_modules/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/**/node_modules/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**/dist/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/**/dist/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**/dist-webview/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/**/dist-webview/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**/.next/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**/.turbo/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/**/.turbo/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**/coverage/**",
        "!$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/**/coverage/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/docs/manual.md",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/docs/faq.md",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/scripts/help-content.mjs",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/scripts/help-quoted-strings-absent.json"
      ]
    },
    // `next-config.test.ts` reads `apps/server/src` to check the shell's config
    // against the server it talks to; `members-styling.test.ts` and
    // `tap-target-density.test.ts` both read `packages/ui/src/ui.css` directly.
    // The second entry is therefore load-bearing rather than tidy: without it, a
    // change to that stylesheet replays a cached GREEN log instead of re-running
    // either test, which is the same class of hole the comment below records for
    // the server suite. Found while adding the second reader, and it is the
    // FIRST reader that was already exposed.
    // (Reviewed 2026-10-02: `ui` is a declared dependency of `web`, and `ui#build`'s
    // hash already covers its `src/`, so the `packages/ui/src/**` entry is redundant
    // today — an equivalent mutant. Kept: it states the reader, and it keeps the hole
    // closed if the dependency is ever dropped.)
    "@gisik-nokma/web#test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "inputs": [
        "$TURBO_DEFAULT$",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/server/src/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/ui/src/**"
      ]
    },
    // The tooling, ci and docs suites assert things that live at the REPO ROOT and
    // nowhere near this package: the gate scripts and their fixtures, the runbook,
    // the compose file, and CI's own workflow. Case 13.208 parses `ci.yml` and
    // asserts its job graph — cached against `apps/server/**` alone, a CI edit that
    // broke the graph would report green.
    //
    // THE SECOND HALF OF THIS LIST (traced 2026-10-02, the release-kind gate caches)
    // is what the original six entries missed — each one a file a server test reads
    // that a change could break with this task still replaying green:
    //   `.env.example`            config.test.ts, expired-sessions.test.ts
    //   `package.json`            node-version.test.ts, compose-dev-contract.test.ts
    //   `deploy/**`               app-spec-ingress, backup-worker-env (`deploy/do/app.yaml`)
    //   `docker-compose*.yml`     compose-dev-contract (the root and hot files, not just dev)
    //   `apps/*/Dockerfile*`      dockerfile-cache-shape reads `apps/web/Dockerfile` and `.dev`
    //   `apps/*/package.json`,    `check-runbook-commands.mjs` reads every workspace manifest,
    //   `packages/*/package.json` including the ones `server` does not depend on
    //   `reference/**`            the seed suites read the frozen convenience-corner board
    //   `apps/web/e2e-stack/**`   e2e-teardown.test.ts imports `helpers/teardown.ts` from there
    //   `apps/web/next.config.ts` security-middleware.test.ts reads the web shell's headers
    // (`web` is not a dependency of `server`, so the last two are invisible to `^build`.)
    // `packages/app-core/src` (client-contract.test.ts) and `packages/domain/src` are
    // also read, but both are declared dependencies of `server`, so turbo already folds
    // their hash in through `^build`.
    "@gisik-nokma/server#test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "inputs": [
        "$TURBO_DEFAULT$",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/scripts/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/docs/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/.github/workflows/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/docker-compose.dev.yml",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/test-cases/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/.env.example",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/package.json",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/deploy/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/docker-compose*.yml",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/*/Dockerfile*",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/*/package.json",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/*/package.json",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/reference/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/e2e-stack/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/web/next.config.ts"
      ]
    },
    // `ticket-editor-slot.test.tsx` and `toolbar-icons-phone.test.tsx` read source in
    // OTHER packages as text and assert on it: `app-core`'s editor slot and phone-board
    // hook, `server`'s attachment sniffer, and `mobile`'s generated webview HTML. None
    // of them is a declared dependency of `editor` (it depends only on `domain`), so
    // the hash could not see them. Declared as directories, not the four files
    // measured: the next test to read a sibling should not be the one that finds out.
    //
    // The ui test helpers are read too, from a package `editor` does not depend on:
    // `editor-css-binding.test.ts`, `toolbar-icons-phone.test.tsx`,
    // `drive-never-inline.test.ts` and `ticket-image.test.ts` import `colour-scan.ts`
    // and `css-rules.ts` from `packages/ui/test/helpers/`. Without that directory a
    // change to `css-rules.ts` replays the CSS-binding suite green. (There is no
    // `packages/ui/test/tsconfig.json` in the tree, so none is declared.)
    "@gisik-nokma/editor#test": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "inputs": [
        "$TURBO_DEFAULT$",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/app-core/src/views/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/server/src/attachments/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/mobile/src/editor/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/ui/test/helpers/**"
      ]
    },
    "typecheck": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"]
    }
  }
}
